{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-103309",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+(-3)\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-3\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=10,$ we get that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-3\\pi )=10.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-3\\pi )=\\frac{1}{2}(10)=5.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
